IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cea-types`

-- Customs and Excise Act 2018 — GOAL 1: CUSTOMS VALUE.
--
--   "What is the Customs value of the imported goods?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2018_4.txt — s 101 and
-- Schedule 4, cls 2-12.

§ `Goal 1 — Customs value`

-- Schedule 4 cl 2(2) "(a) persons are related if— (i) they are officers or
-- directors of one another's business; or (ii) they are legally recognised
-- partners in business; or (iii) they are employer and employee; or (iv) any
-- person directly or indirectly owns, controls, or holds 5% or more of the
-- outstanding voting stock or shares of both of them; or (v) one of them
-- directly or indirectly controls the other; or (vi) both of them are
-- directly or indirectly controlled by a third person; or (vii) together
-- they directly or indirectly control a third person; or (viii) they are
-- members of the same family".
@ref Schedule 4 cl 2(2)(a)
GIVEN p IS A `Buyer and seller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `are related` p IF
        p's `officers or directors of one another's business`
    OR  p's `legally recognised partners in business`
    OR  p's `employer and employee`
    OR  p's `largest share of both held by one person, in percent` AT LEAST 5
    OR  p's `one controls the other`
    OR  p's `both controlled by a third person`
    OR  p's `together they control a third person`
    OR  p's `members of the same family`

-- Schedule 4 cl 5 "The transaction value can be used ... only if— (a) there
-- are no restrictions respecting the disposition or use of the goods by the
-- buyer, other than [those imposed by law, geographical, or not substantially
-- affecting value]; and (b) neither the sale ... nor the price ... is subject
-- to some condition or consideration in respect of which a value cannot be
-- determined; and (c) [resale proceeds to the seller are included or can be
-- adjusted]; and (d) the buyer and seller are not related ... or, if they are
-- related ..., the importer complies with clause 6 if required". cl 4(2):
-- methods 2 to 6 also apply if a required cl 7(b) adjustment cannot be made
-- for lack of sufficient information, or the chief executive doubts the
-- declared value.
@ref Schedule 4 cls 4(2), 5
GIVEN t IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction value can be used` t IF
        NOT t's `restrictions on disposition or use other than permitted ones`
    AND NOT t's `sale or price subject to a condition that cannot be valued`
    AND NOT t's `resale proceeds to the seller neither included nor adjustable`
    AND ((NOT `are related` (t's `buyer and seller`)) OR t's `clause 6 complied with or not required`)
    AND NOT t's `a required addition lacks sufficient information`
    AND NOT t's `the chief executive doubts the declared value`

-- Schedule 4 cl 7 "The transaction value ... is to be calculated by— (a)
-- taking the price paid or payable ...; and (b) ... adding amounts (to the
-- extent that each amount is not included in the price ...) ...; and (c) ...
-- deducting amounts (to the extent that each amount is included in the
-- price ...) ...; and (d) in respect of carrier media bearing data or
-- instructions, deducting the value of the data or instructions if— (i) the
-- value ... is distinguished from the cost or value of the carrier media; and
-- (ii) the data or instructions are not incorporated in data processing
-- equipment." cl 3: interest under a financing arrangement meeting its
-- conditions "is not to be regarded as part of the Customs value".
@ref Schedule 4 cls 3, 7
@export The transaction value of imported goods under Schedule 4, clause 7 of the Customs and Excise Act 2018 (NZ): the price paid or payable, plus the clause 7(b) amounts not already in it (commissions, packing, buyer's assists, royalties, resale proceeds, repairs, transport and insurance to export), less the clause 7(c) amounts in it (later transport, post-import services, New Zealand duties and taxes), less separately valued data on carrier media and qualifying financing interest (clause 3). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Transaction facts`  @desc The price, the clause 7(b) additions and 7(c) deductions, carrier media data, and financing interest
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transaction value of` t MEANS
        t's `price paid or payable`
    PLUS sum (t's `additions under clause 7(b)`)
    MINUS (sum (t's `deductions under clause 7(c)`) PLUS media PLUS interest)
    WHERE
        media MEANS IF t's `data distinguished and not in data processing equipment` THEN t's `value of data or instructions on carrier media` ELSE 0
        interest MEANS IF t's `interest meets clause 3` THEN t's `interest included in the price` ELSE 0

-- Schedule 4 cl 4 "(1) The primary basis for determining the Customs value
-- of imported goods is the transaction value ... (3) The chief executive may
-- determine the Customs value ... by proceeding sequentially through methods
-- 2 to 6". cl 9 "(2) If there are 2 or more transaction values of identical
-- goods that meet all the requirements ..., the Customs value ... must be
-- determined on the basis of the lowest such transaction value". cls 11-12:
-- likewise for similar goods. Methods 4 to 6 are not encoded.
@ref s 101; Schedule 4 cls 4, 9-12
@export The Customs value of imported goods under s 101 and Schedule 4 of the Customs and Excise Act 2018 (NZ): the transaction value where clause 5 allows it (no restrictions or unvaluable conditions, resale proceeds accounted for, buyer and seller unrelated or clause 6 met, adjustments supported and the value not doubted); otherwise the lowest qualifying transaction value of identical goods, then of similar goods; methods 4 to 6 are not encoded (refused). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Transaction facts`  @desc The transaction, the relationship between buyer and seller, and any comparable transaction values of identical or similar goods
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Customs value of` t MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transaction value can be used` t THEN `the transaction value of` t
        IF NOT null (t's `transaction values of identical goods`) THEN minimum (t's `transaction values of identical goods`)
        IF NOT null (t's `transaction values of similar goods`) THEN minimum (t's `transaction values of similar goods`)
        OTHERWISE `methods 4 to 6 of Schedule 4 are not encoded`

`methods 4 to 6 of Schedule 4 are not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 4 methods 4 to 6 (deductive, computed and fallback values) are not encoded"
